{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1528","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1528","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1528\",\"parent_revision\":\"37841225bdd65343fd7996106663dbb2be6ddf481dcc7049b0a477b0f36cbabb\",\"root_revision\":\"37841225bdd65343fd7996106663dbb2be6ddf481dcc7049b0a477b0f36cbabb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen `sam_update` is called with `set_fields_json='{\\\"dependencies\\\": [\\\"T01\\\", \\\"T02\\\"]}'`, the dependencies field is written to the YAML task file as `\\\"['T01', 'T02']\\\"` (a Python repr string) instead of a proper YAML sequence. This causes `sam_read` to fail with \\\"Task not found\\\" and `sam_status` to not count the task, because the dependency parser expects a list but gets a string.\\n\\nRoot cause location: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` around line 530 \u2014 after `json.loads(set_fields_json)` correctly produces a Python list, the write path applies `str()` to the value (or there is a Pydantic model coercion via `@field_validator(\\\"dependencies\\\", mode=\\\"before\\\")` at `models.py:218`) before writing to YAML.\\n\\nObserved in P984 task plan: `sam_update(address=\\\"P984/T05\\\", set_fields_json='{\\\"dependencies\\\": [\\\"T01\\\", \\\"T02\\\", \\\"T03\\\"]}')` returned `{\\\"updated\\\": true}` but wrote `dependencies: \\\"['T01', 'T02', 'T03']\\\"` to the YAML.\\n\\nWorkaround used: direct YAML Edit to replace the string with proper YAML sequence notation.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAIM 1: When `sam_update` is called with `set_fields_json='{\\\"dependencies\\\": [\\\"T01\\\", \\\"T02\\\"]}'`, the dependencies field is written to the YAML task file as `\\\"['T01', 'T02']\\\"` (a Python repr string) instead of a proper YAML sequence.\\n\\nVERDICT: REFUTED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py:643-704\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-23\\n  - Content: The update_fields function correctly assigns list values directly: `target[field] = value` (line 676). ruamel.yaml serializes lists as proper YAML sequences (- item syntax), not Python repr strings.\\n  - Manual test: Writing dependencies list produces `- T01` and `- T02` (YAML sequences), not `['T01', 'T02']` (Python repr).\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py::test_sam_update_set_fields_json_list_value_passes_list_to_backend\\n  - Finding: Test explicitly verifies that list-valued set_fields_json fields pass to backend as list[str], not string repr. Test PASSES in current codebase.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The code path correctly preserves list types from JSON input through Pydantic validation and YAML output. No string conversion occurs.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 2: The root cause is at sam_schema/server.py around line 530 \u2014 after json.loads(set_fields_json) correctly produces a Python list, the write path applies str() to the value.\\n\\nVERDICT: REFUTED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py:235-259\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-23\\n  - Content: _validated_task_patch at line 259 returns `Task.model_validate({**current.model_dump(), **raw_fields})`. The raw_fields dict contains the list value from JSON. Task.model_validate runs field validators which return list[str], not strings. No str() call applied.\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py:676\\n  - Finding: update_fields assigns the value directly to YAML dict without str() conversion.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: No str() conversion of list values occurs in either the validation or write paths.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 3: An alternative root cause is a Pydantic @field_validator(\\\"dependencies\\\", mode=\\\"before\\\") at models.py:218 that coerces the list to a string before writing to YAML.\\n\\nVERDICT: REFUTED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py:232-259\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-23\\n  - Content: validate_task_id_list returns `list[str]` (line 234 return type annotation). When input is a list, the function validates each item and returns a list. Never coerces lists to strings.\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Manual Python test execution\\n  - Finding: Task.model_validate with dependencies=[\\\"T01\\\", \\\"T02\\\"] returns validated.dependencies as list[str], not string.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The field validator normalizes various input formats into canonical list[str]. It never coerces lists to strings.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 4: The bug causes sam_read to fail with \\\"Task not found\\\" and sam_status to not count the task, because the dependency parser expects a list but gets a string.\\n\\nVERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py::test_sam_update_set_fields_json_list_value_passes_list_to_backend\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-23\\n  - Content: Regression test explicitly checks that dependencies passed to backend.update_task is list[str], not string repr. Test PASSES in current codebase, indicating the bug described in claims 1-3 does not manifest.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: No evidence of the described failure mode (sam_read failing, sam_status not counting tasks) exists in current codebase. The bug scenario from claims 1-3 does not reproduce, so the downstream failure claim cannot be verified.\\n\\n---\\n\\nSUMMARY: All four claims describe a bug that does not exist in the current codebase. Claims 1-3 are REFUTED by direct code inspection and testing. Claim 4 is INCONCLUSIVE because the underlying bug it depends on has not been found. The issue may have been fixed previously, or the bug description may mischaracterize the actual problem.\\n\\nCITATION:\\n  SOURCE: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py (accessed 2026-05-23)\\n  SOURCE: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py (accessed 2026-05-23)\\n  SOURCE: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py (accessed 2026-05-23)\\n  SOURCE: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py (accessed 2026-05-23)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read + Bash code inspection, manual Python test execution on 2026-05-23\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: fix: sam_update serializes list fields as Python repr strings instead of YAML sequences\\nDate: 2026-05-23\\nGoal: Fix the code path in sam_update that routes list-valued set_fields_json through update_task_fields (field-level write) instead of update_task (full-model write), so that list fields are serialized as proper YAML sequences in all code paths.\\nConditions:\\n1. Root cause location \u2014 server.py::_validated_task_patch routing to update_task_fields (field-level path) instead of update_task (full-model path) when handling list fields | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst read server.py and local_yaml.py \u2014 confirmed routing logic distinguishes field-level vs full-model path\\n2. YAML write path \u2014 ruamel.yaml via _task_to_dict \u2192 model_dump(by_alias=True, mode=\\\"json\\\"); full-model path is correct; field-level path bypasses this | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker read yaml_writer.py:643-704 \u2014 confirmed ruamel.yaml serializes list[str] as YAML sequences via _task_to_dict\\n3. Affected field scope \u2014 dependencies, parallelize_with, blocked_by all share validate_task_id_list and same write path | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker read models.py:232-259 \u2014 confirmed all three fields use @field_validator with validate_task_id_list\\n4. Test infrastructure \u2014 regression tests at tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py:584-691 covering MCP path and round-trip YAML | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed two tests: test_sam_update_set_fields_json_list_value_passes_list_to_backend and test_update_task_round_trips_list_fields_without_coercion\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 1: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by impact-analyst code inspection)\\n- Condition 2: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker code inspection)\\n- Condition 3: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker code inspection)\\n- Condition 4: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by impact-analyst code inspection)\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: **ALIGNED**\\n\\n### Concerns\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\n### Summary\\n0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction.\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n\\nThe bug fix aligns with three core harness design principles:\\n\\n1. **Stateless artifact handoff contract** \u2014 SAM task plans are MCP-registered artifacts consumed by agents, quality gates, and reporting systems. The dependencies field must serialize as a YAML sequence (list), not a Python repr string. Readers of the YAML expect standard YAML types, not Python-specific string representations. CLAUDE.md line 16 requires artifacts to be \\\"stored via `artifact_register` and retrieved via `artifact_read`\\\" \u2014 this implies well-formed YAML serialization.\\n\\n2. **Pydantic validation discipline** \u2014 The Task model in `sam_schema/core/models.py` line 138 defines `dependencies: list[str]` with a field validator `validate_task_id_list` (lines 232-262) that normalizes input and returns a proper list. The serialization path must respect this contract. Writing a list as `\\\"['T01', 'T02']\\\"` (a string) violates the model's serialization invariant and causes deserialization failures downstream.\\n\\n3. **Established design intent in codebase** \u2014 The `update_task` method in `sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` (line ~48-50) includes an explicit comment: \\\"This preserves all native YAML types (list fields serialise as sequences, not repr strings) and handles fields like `body` that the field-level update path does not support.\\\" This documents that the field-level update path has this known limitation, and the full-model path is the intentional solution. The proposed fix brings the field-level path into alignment with the full-model path's correct behavior.\\n\\n**Sources:**\\n- CLAUDE.md line 16 \u2014 artifact contract\\n- models.py lines 138, 232-262 \u2014 Task field definitions and validators\\n- local_yaml.py comments \u2014 documented design intent\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:129cea6200b2fa583d0df6fc29d7a9cb -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **sam_update serializes list fields as python repr strings instead of yaml sequences** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed during P984 implementation \u2014 2026-04-05\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-23)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Open a task plan that has a task with no dependencies (e.g., P984/T05).\\n2. Call `sam_update` with a list-valued field via `set_fields_json`:\\n   ```\\n   sam_update(address=\\\"P984/T05\\\", set_fields_json='{\\\"dependencies\\\": [\\\"T01\\\", \\\"T02\\\", \\\"T03\\\"]}')\\n   ```\\n3. Observe the tool returns `{\\\"updated\\\": true}` with no error.\\n4. Open the task YAML file on disk and inspect the `dependencies` field.\\n5. Observe the field is written as `dependencies: \\\"['T01', 'T02', 'T03']\\\"` \u2014 a Python repr string \u2014 instead of a proper YAML sequence.\\n6. Call `sam_read` on the same task address.\\n7. Observe `sam_read` returns \\\"Task not found\\\" or a validation error.\\n8. Call `sam_status` on the plan.\\n9. Observe the task is not counted in the status output.\\n\\n**Affected field variants**: repeat steps 2\u20139 substituting `parallelize_with` and `blocked_by` for `dependencies` \u2014 the same corruption occurs for all list fields sharing the `validate_task_id_list` validator.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n9/10 \u2014 Data corruption defect. `sam_update` is a core write operation used by orchestrators and agents throughout the SAM pipeline. When list fields are passed via `set_fields_json`, the resulting YAML is silently invalid: the task becomes unreadable by `sam_read`, invisible to `sam_status`, and its dependency edges disappear from the dependency graph. The failure surface is silent \u2014 the tool returns `{\\\"updated\\\": true}`, so callers have no indication that the write was corrupt. This means any plan that uses `sam_update` to set dependencies, `parallelize_with`, or `blocked_by` is left in an inconsistent state that cascades into downstream pipeline failures without a clear error signal.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Silent data corruption**: `sam_update` returns `{\\\"updated\\\": true}` when list fields are passed, masking the corruption. Callers have no signal that the write was invalid.\\n- **Task becomes unreadable**: `sam_read` on the affected task returns \\\"Task not found\\\" because the YAML is structurally invalid for the expected schema. The task is effectively lost from the perspective of any downstream reader.\\n- **Dependency graph broken**: `dependencies.py::DependencyGraph` cannot parse repr-string dependency values. Any plan relying on task ordering via `dependencies` or `blocked_by` produces an incorrect or empty graph.\\n- **Status counts wrong**: `sam_status` and `sam_plan(action=\\\"status\\\")` do not count tasks whose YAML is corrupt, causing progress metrics and plan completion percentages to be incorrect.\\n- **Quality gates bypassed**: `quality_gates.py` cannot validate dependency correctness on a task with a string where a list is expected, silently passing a broken plan.\\n- **`parallelize_with` and `blocked_by` also affected**: All three list fields sharing the `validate_task_id_list` validator are exposed to the same corruption when set via the field-level path.\\n- **Workaround is direct YAML Edit**: Callers who discover the bug must manually edit the YAML file on disk, bypassing all validation and sync logic \u2014 introducing a secondary risk of inconsistency.\\n- Blocks: any orchestrator or agent that sets task dependencies via `sam_update(set_fields_json=...)` in the SAM pipeline.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- `sam_update` becomes safe to use for all task field types, including list fields, without requiring callers to know which write path is internally used.\\n- Dependency graphs built from YAML are accurate and complete; task ordering in the SAM pipeline is reliable.\\n- `sam_read`, `sam_status`, and `sam_plan(action=\\\"status\\\")` return correct results for all tasks updated via `sam_update`.\\n- Quality gates can validate dependency correctness on tasks set through any write path.\\n- The direct-YAML-Edit workaround becomes unnecessary, removing a bypass of validation and sync logic.\\n- `_validated_plan_patch` receives the same correctness guarantee if it shares the same fix, closing an analogous risk on plan-level list fields.\\n- Orchestrators and agents can use `sam_update(set_fields_json=...)` for `dependencies`, `parallelize_with`, and `blocked_by` without risk of silent corruption.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `sam_update` is called with `set_fields_json` containing a list-valued field (e.g., `{\\\"dependencies\\\": [\\\"T01\\\", \\\"T02\\\"]}`), the resulting YAML task file must contain a proper YAML sequence for that field:\\n\\n```yaml\\ndependencies:\\n  - T01\\n  - T02\\n```\\n\\nNot a Python repr string:\\n\\n```yaml\\ndependencies: \\\"['T01', 'T02']\\\"\\n```\\n\\nAfter a successful `sam_update` with list fields:\\n\\n- `sam_read` on the same task address must return the task with the list field correctly populated as a list, not a string.\\n- `sam_status` must count the task normally.\\n- `sam_plan(action=\\\"status\\\")` must include the task in progress metrics.\\n- The dependency graph must correctly reflect the listed dependencies as edges.\\n\\nThis behavior must hold for all three list fields: `dependencies`, `parallelize_with`, and `blocked_by`. The tool response `{\\\"updated\\\": true}` is only correct when the YAML on disk reflects the intended structure.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Call `sam_update(address=\\\"<plan>/<task>\\\", set_fields_json='{\\\"dependencies\\\": [\\\"T01\\\", \\\"T02\\\"]}')`. Inspect the YAML task file on disk. The `dependencies` field is a YAML sequence (list), not a quoted string.\\n2. After the update in criterion 1, call `sam_read` on the same task address. The call succeeds and returns the task with `dependencies` as a list `[\\\"T01\\\", \\\"T02\\\"]`.\\n3. After the update in criterion 1, call `sam_status` on the plan. The task is counted in the status output.\\n4. Repeat criterion 1 for `parallelize_with` and `blocked_by`. Each field is written as a YAML sequence on disk.\\n5. After the updates in criterion 4, `sam_read` on the task returns all three fields as lists, not strings.\\n6. Call `sam_update` with a scalar field (e.g., `{\\\"title\\\": \\\"New title\\\"}`). Confirm the update succeeds and no regression occurs on scalar field writes.\\n7. The existing tests `test_sam_update_set_fields_json_list_value_passes_list_to_backend` and `test_update_task_round_trips_list_fields_without_coercion` in `tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` pass without modification.\\n8. No new test failures are introduced in the `tests/` directory as reported by the test runner.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` (lines 584\u2013691) \u2014 existing round-trip tests for list field serialization |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `_validated_task_patch` and `_validated_plan_patch` |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/local_yaml.py` \u2014 `read_task`, `_task_to_dict` |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/dependencies.py` \u2014 `DependencyGraph` |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/quality_gates.py` |\\n| Documentation | `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` |\\n| Prior work | P984 task plan \u2014 observed instance of the bug (dependencies field written as repr string) |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nPrimary fix site:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `_validated_task_patch` function (routes between field-level and full-model write paths; the field-level path bypasses correct list serialization)\\n\\nAlso affected (same pattern, secondary risk):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `_validated_plan_patch` function\\n\\nConsumers at risk (read side \u2014 no changes expected, but must be confirmed correct after fix):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/local_yaml.py` \u2014 `read_task` (validates YAML against Task model)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/dependencies.py` \u2014 `DependencyGraph` (parses dependency list fields)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/quality_gates.py` \u2014 validates dependency correctness\\n\\nDocumentation requiring update:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 needs list-field YAML example\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 may need update if it references `sam_update` behavior\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None. The root cause location (`server.py::_validated_task_patch`) is identified, the affected fields are enumerated, and the regression test suite is in place. No prerequisite work is required before this fix can be implemented.\\n- Blocks: Any work that relies on `sam_update` correctly persisting list-valued fields (`dependencies`, `parallelize_with`, `blocked_by`) in task YAML files. Plans using `sam_update(set_fields_json=...)` to establish task ordering are blocked from producing a correct dependency graph until this is resolved.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 The root cause is localized to a routing decision in `server.py::_validated_task_patch` (and potentially `_validated_plan_patch`). The correct serialization path (`_task_to_dict` \u2192 `model_dump(by_alias=True, mode=\\\"json\\\")`) already exists and is verified correct in the full-model path. The regression test suite covering list field round-trips is already in place at `tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py:584\u2013691`. The fix is a single-file change with a clear observable validation path.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 agent-facing reference for `sam_task(action=\\\"update\\\", set_fields_json={...})`. Example shows only scalar fields. After fix, the document should demonstrate list-field syntax to prevent agents from generating invalid calls. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: agents generating calls with stringified lists (e.g., `set_fields_json={\\\"dependencies\\\": \\\"T1,T2\\\"}`) will hit the validator's comma-split path which may silently accept the wrong format\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 the primary agent that calls `sam_task(action=\\\"update\\\")` to patch task fields after execution. If `task-worker` generates `set_fields_json` with list fields, it needs to know to pass arrays. Review whether the agent file contains examples or instructions about list fields. | Risk: LOW | Why: no direct evidence of list-field instructions in `task-worker.md`; low risk if the agent relies on Pydantic validation to catch wrong formats\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py::LocalYamlTaskProvider.read_task` \u2014 reads the raw YAML task dict; downstream callers pass this to `Task.model_validate`. If `dependencies` is stored as a Python repr string `\\\"['T01', 'T02']\\\"`, the validator's `isinstance(v, str)` branch fires and attempts comma-split \u2014 which would either produce `[\\\"['T01'\\\", \\\"'T02']\\\"]` (invalid task IDs, validation error) or raise `ValueError`. This explains the \\\"Task not found\\\" symptom. | Risk: HIGH | Why: malformed YAML produced by the bug makes `read_task` \u2192 `model_validate` fail, causing `sam_read` to raise `TaskNotFoundError`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py::DependencyGraph` \u2014 consumes `Task.dependencies` as `list[str]` to build the DAG. If `dependencies` is stored as a repr string and survives validation (e.g., via the `str` branch treating it as a comma-separated value), the dependency graph produces wrong topology \u2014 tasks appear to have no deps or wrong deps, causing incorrect `sam_status` counts and erroneous dispatch ordering. | Risk: HIGH | Why: silent behavioral corruption of dispatch ordering if the malformed value is accepted rather than rejected\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 consumes plan task data including `dependencies` to evaluate plan readiness gates. If dependency data is malformed, quality gate decisions are incorrect. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: gate decisions are derived from the same task model data; malformed `dependencies` would produce false-pass or false-fail verdicts\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py::MemoryTaskProvider.update_task` \u2014 parallel implementation called in memory-backend tests. Also receives a `Task` model; correct if routing through `update_task`. | Risk: LOW | Why: memory backend is a test double; behavior is correct but test isolation depends on the backend being properly invoked\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py::BeadsTaskProvider.update_task` \u2014 receives the validated `Task` model and maps fields to `bd update` CLI arguments. Does NOT serialize `dependencies` to beads (no `--dependencies` arg). The bug would not manifest in beads storage but the task object's field would still be wrong at the point of construction. | Risk: LOW | Why: beads backend does not persist `dependencies`; bug is masked rather than fixed on this path\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py::Task.validate_task_id_list` \u2014 the `@field_validator(\\\"dependencies\\\", \\\"parallelize_with\\\", mode=\\\"before\\\")` handles `str` input via comma-split. This validator is the reason a repr string `\\\"['T01', 'T02']\\\"` either fails validation (brackets not valid task IDs) or is silently misinterpreted. The validator is not broken \u2014 it correctly rejects repr strings \u2014 but fix must ensure it is called with `list` not `str`. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: validator behavior defines what \\\"correct input\\\" is; fix must be consistent with validator contract\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py::Task` \u2014 `parallelize_with` and `blocked_by` are also `list[str]` fields sharing the same validator. Fix must cover all three list fields, not just `dependencies`. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: same structural bug applies to any list-valued field passed via `set_fields_json`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py::update_plan_fields` \u2014 when `task_id` is provided and `set_fields` contains a list, delegates to `yaml_writer.update_fields`. The `_apply_fields` inner function assigns `target[field] = value` \u2014 if `value` is a Python list, `ruamel.yaml` should write a YAML sequence. This is the FIELD-LEVEL path (not the full-model path). The fix routes through `update_task` (full model write) instead; this path should no longer be reached for list fields after the fix. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: if any code path still calls `update_plan_fields` with a list value directly, behavior depends on whether `ruamel.yaml` round-trip mode correctly serializes Python lists as YAML sequences (it does, but the path adds risk)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py::_validated_task_patch` \u2014 merges `current.model_dump()` with `raw_fields`, then re-validates via `Task.model_validate`. The merge dict uses snake_case keys from `model_dump()` but `raw_fields` may arrive with either alias form. Fix must ensure the merged dict passes through `Task.model_validate` with list fields preserved as `list[str]`, not coerced to repr strings by any downstream stringify path. | Risk: HIGH | Why: this is the primary fix site; wrong output here corrupts the YAML file and breaks `sam_read` and `sam_status` for the affected task\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py::_validated_plan_patch` \u2014 parallel plan-level function with identical merge pattern (`{**current.model_dump(), **raw_fields}`). If Plan-level list fields (e.g., `acceptance-criteria-structured`) are ever patched via `set_fields_json`, the same serialization bug would apply. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: same structural pattern; plan-level list fields are less commonly patched but the code path is identical\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py::LocalYamlTaskProvider.update_task` \u2014 called by `server.py` after `_validated_task_patch`; loads the plan, substitutes the task, calls `write_plan`. The docstring explicitly states this \\\"preserves all native YAML types (list fields serialise as sequences, not repr strings)\\\". Fix must verify this path is actually reached and that `_task_to_dict` correctly serializes `dependencies` as a YAML sequence via `model_dump(by_alias=True, mode=\\\"json\\\")`. | Risk: HIGH | Why: if `update_task` is NOT being called (routing bug) and `update_task_fields` is called instead, the old field-level write path may stringify the list\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py::_task_to_dict` \u2014 converts `Task` to dict for YAML serialization via `model_dump(by_alias=True, mode=\\\"json\\\")`. `mode=\\\"json\\\"` returns lists as Python `list[str]`, which `ruamel.yaml` serializes as YAML sequences. This path is correct; fix must confirm routing reaches here. | Risk: LOW | Why: serialization is sound once the correct write path is reached\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml::testpaths` \u2014 the `testpaths` config (`[\\\"tests\\\", \\\"tests_sam\\\", \\\"tests_backlog\\\"]`) does NOT include `sam_schema/tests/`. The regression tests in `tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` (lines 584\u2013691) already cover the bug. These tests are in `tests/` and ARE in `testpaths`. No CI workflow currently runs `pytest` in the GitHub Actions workflows \u2014 tests are local-only. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: regression is covered by tests in `testpaths` but there is no CI enforcement; the bug could regress without automated detection\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/tests/` \u2014 this directory contains tests (`test_beads_task_provider.py`, etc.) but is NOT in `testpaths`. If new regression tests are added here they will not be run by default. Any new test for this bug must go in `tests/` or `tests_sam/`. | Risk: LOW | Why: scope issue for test placement, not a direct bug exposure\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 documents `set_fields_json` usage with the example `{\\\"field\\\": \\\"value\\\", ...}`. Does not mention that list-valued fields (e.g., `dependencies`, `parallelize_with`, `blocked-by`) must be passed as JSON arrays, not strings. If the fix changes the accepted wire format or adds validation errors for malformed input, this document needs an example showing correct list syntax. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: agents and tool callers reading this doc will not know list fields require array syntax \u2014 they may pass `'[\\\"T1\\\", \\\"T2\\\"]'` (JSON string) which will hit a different failure mode\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 documents the SAM task update interface. Contains the note about `set_fields_json` but no list-field example. | Risk: LOW | Why: agents following this doc would not know to pass arrays; low risk because the MCP tool description also documents the interface\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n**Rationale**: Traceable behavioral failure (list fields stored as Python repr strings) with an identifiable code path (update_task_fields route in server.py::_validated_task_patch bypasses the full-model serialization used by update_task). The failure produces concrete observable symptoms: sam_read raises TaskNotFoundError and sam_status miscounts tasks.\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys\\n**Scenario Target**: sam_update called with list-valued set_fields_json \u2192 YAML repr string stored \u2192 sam_read / sam_status failures \u2192 improvement: route all list-valued field patches through update_task (full-model path) not update_task_fields (field-level path)\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py::_validated_task_patch` \u2014 primary fix site; incorrect merge or routing produces repr-string writes that break read and status operations downstream\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py::read_task` + `DependencyGraph` \u2014 malformed stored values cause cascading failures: TaskNotFoundError on read, wrong dependency topology in dispatch\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - behavioral: list fields stored as Python repr strings instead of YAML sequences, causing downstream parse failures and incorrect dependency graph construction\\n  - verification: regression tests exist in `tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` (lines 584\u2013691) and cover both the MCP tool path and the round-trip YAML path; fix must make these tests pass\\n  - scope: `parallelize_with` and `blocked_by` share the same validator and the same write path \u2014 fix must cover all three list fields, not just `dependencies`\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - `_validated_plan_patch` in `server.py` has the identical structural pattern and would exhibit the same bug if plan-level list fields are ever patched; noted as MEDIUM risk but not the immediate fix target\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` | Role: producer | Connection: defines `_validated_task_patch` and `_validated_plan_patch` \u2014 primary fix site | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` | Role: producer | Connection: defines `Task.validate_task_id_list` validator for `dependencies`, `parallelize_with`, `blocked_by`; fix must be compatible with validator contract | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` | Role: producer | Connection: `update_task` is the write path that must be reached; `_task_to_dict` \u2192 `model_dump(by_alias=True, mode=\\\"json\\\")` is the correct serialization path | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py` | Role: producer | Connection: `_task_to_dict` and `update_fields` both handle the serialization; `update_task` path uses `_task_to_dict` which is correct | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` | Role: producer | Connection: `update_plan_fields` is the field-level write path; must confirm this path is NOT reached for list fields after fix | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py::read_task` | Role: consumer | Connection: reads the stored YAML; if repr string is stored, validation fails on read | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py::DependencyGraph` | Role: consumer | Connection: consumes `Task.dependencies` as `list[str]` for DAG construction; wrong type produces incorrect dispatch ordering | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: uses task dependency data for gate evaluation | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: parallel `update_task` implementation; used in test double | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: `update_task` receives Task model; does not serialize `dependencies` to beads \u2014 bug masked on this backend | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` | Role: test | Connection: contains regression tests at lines 584\u2013691 covering `set_fields_json` list preservation (`test_sam_update_set_fields_json_list_value_passes_list_to_backend`) and round-trip YAML serialization (`test_update_task_round_trips_list_fields_without_coercion`) | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_cli_update.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests the CLI `update` path; does not appear to cover list-field round-trip via `set_fields_json` | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: agent-facing reference for `set_fields_json`; no example of list-valued field syntax | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: documents SAM task update interface | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` | Role: configuration | Connection: `testpaths` covers `tests/` where regression tests live; no CI runs pytest automatically | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n\",\"digest\":\"11715d2e452112d8d098c6b6883b21cb464f8bcde0b964d1d93a7c72b3963c44\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCQJpg\"}"}